IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei2-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), s 55(2) to (4): alternative methods of establishing a person's hours of
-- insurable employment. Piece ei2. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30. Seat: the claimant (as an employee who may be a party to an agreement).
--
-- Section 54 (regulations of 45 paragraphs) and s 55(1) (regulations on how many hours of insurable employment a person has)
-- are regulation-making powers: inert machinery, listed one row each in the coverage table of NOTES.md. Their content
-- is in the Regulations (hours of insurable employment: regs 9.1 to 11, piece er1).
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld). Each subsection is a power of the Commission over the way a person's hours are counted: the person
-- (a claimant, an employer or an employee) is liable to the alternative method (s 55(2), (3)); an employer or an employee who
-- agrees holds a power of agreement and is then liable to the agreed method until the Commission rescinds it (s 55(4)).
-- What the Commission "considers" is a BOOLEAN input.

§ `Section 55 - alternative methods`

-- (2): "If the Commission considers that it is not possible to apply the provisions of the regulations, it may authorize an
-- alternative method of establishing how many hours of insurable employment a person has."
-- src:1042 | Alternative methods
-- src:1043 | (2) If the Commission considers that it is not possible to apply the provisions of the regulations, it may authorize an alternative method of establishing how many hours of insurable employment a person has.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 55(2) (src:1042-1043)
GIVEN `the Commission considers that it is not possible to apply the provisions of the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 55(2) the Commission may authorize an alternative method of establishing how many hours of insurable employment a person has` IF
    `the Commission considers that it is not possible to apply the provisions of the regulations`

-- (3): "The Commission may at any time alter the authorized method or rescind the authorization, subject to any conditions
-- that it considers appropriate." Only an authorization already given can be altered or rescinded.
-- src:1044 | Alteration or rescission of authorization
-- src:1045 | (3) The Commission may at any time alter the authorized method or rescind the authorization, subject to any conditions that it considers appropriate.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 55(3) (src:1044-1045)
GIVEN `an alternative method has been authorized under subsection 55(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 55(3) the Commission may alter the authorized method or rescind the authorization` IF
    `an alternative method has been authorized under subsection 55(2)`

-- (4): "The Commission may enter into agreements with employers or employees to provide for alternative methods of
-- establishing how many hours of insurable employment persons have and the Commission may at any time rescind the
-- agreements."
-- src:1046 | Agreement to provide alternative methods
-- src:1047 | (4) The Commission may enter into agreements with employers or employees to provide for alternative methods of establishing how many hours of insurable employment persons have and the Commission may at any time rescind the agreements.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 55(4) (src:1046-1047)
GIVEN `the other party is an employer or an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement provides for an alternative method of establishing how many hours of insurable employment persons have` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 55(4) the Commission may enter into the agreement` IF
        `the other party is an employer or an employee`
    AND `the agreement provides for an alternative method of establishing how many hours of insurable employment persons have`

-- src:1046 | Agreement to provide alternative methods
-- src:1047 | (4) The Commission may enter into agreements with employers or employees to provide for alternative methods of establishing how many hours of insurable employment persons have and the Commission may at any time rescind the agreements.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 55(4) (src:1046-1047)
GIVEN `an agreement has been made under subsection 55(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 55(4) the Commission may rescind the agreement` IF
    `an agreement has been made under subsection 55(4)`
